    "summary": "Strong China>Rider segue and fiery Truckin'>Eyes with solid second set",
    "blurb": "The Spectrum show shines on the China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition and a scorching Truckin' into Eyes of the World pairing. Sugar Magnolia closes the night with upbeat vigor. Both soundboard and matrix sources capture the performance, though the matrix is muddy at the start.",
    "review": "September 20, 1973 at The Spectrum finds the Dead in fine form, delivering a set that balances tight songcraft with adventurous jams. The first set builds momentum toward a standout China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue, where Jerry’s lead lines sparkle over Phil’s steady bass and Keith’s tasteful fills. After a brief, murky audience intro, the matrix recording clears up to showcase the band’s chemistry. In the second set, Truckin' launches into an inspired jam that seamlessly morphs into Eyes of the World, delivering one of the night’s most compelling improvisational peaks. The set rounds out with a bright Stella Blue and a rousing Sugar Magnolia that leaves the audience buzzing. While a surprise horn section on the soundboard tape draws mixed reactions, the overall energy remains high, making this show a solid entry in the 1973 catalog.",
